  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking syntax and terminology redesign for collection and spreading. Source migration: `items...` becomes `*items`, and both `spread(items)` and `items.spread` become `items*`. There are no compatibility aliases, and `spread` is an ordinary identifier with no reserved meaning. The star now has three purely syntactic roles: prefix `*` is the collect marker in binding patterns (`*items` declares a collecting binding; in a parameter list it is a collecting parameter), postfix `*` directly attached to a completed expression is the spread marker (`value*` contributes the value's items to the surrounding item supply), and every other star is multiplication. A star with a same-line right operand multiplies regardless of spacing, so `a* b` is `a * b` — write `a*, b` to spread before another same-line item. Chained spread is `value**`, and the fluent chain `x.Calculate*.Target` lowers to `Target(x.Calculate*)`. Canonical terminology: \"collecting parameter\" is the construct name; \"variadic\" now only describes a callable that accepts a variable number of argument items. Public API: ParameterKind.Variadic→Collecting, CollectingMarkerSpan→CollectMarkerSpan, SequenceSpread.IntrinsicNameSpan→SpreadMarkerSpan, PropertyParameterInfo.IsVariadic→IsCollecting, AstWalker.VisitCollectingBindingMarker→VisitCollectMarker, the ParameterPattern/CallableSignature/CallableBindingPlan variadic members→Collecting*, and TokenKind.Ellipsis was removed. Semantics (capture/collect/spread, exact lists, one-boundary spread) are unchanged and remain Lean-aligned.",
